      "pack": "pack:roadmap",
      "title": "The Protocol's roadmap",
      "framing": "The Protocol's next work, first entry first. The order is a preference: it dates, gates and sequences nothing, and what each entry still needs is read from the graph each time. Until the roadmap priority decision is ratified and its manifest field built, this is an ordinary Pack, and its order is the proposed priority only because this note says so.\n\nFirst come the lead features of the roadmaps and slices arc, whose other Specs are in that arc's Pack. Then the two steps a reader of the Studio's pages could not take, the words of a test line that checks a declaration and an outside register's entries, and then the composed-intent model the build backlog holds. What the first adopter's mass update asks for joins as its captures land. An entry leaves when the pull request that builds it merges.",
      "order": "reading",
